What this means for forks and self-hosted instances
---------------------------------------------------

Privee must stay free and open source software. The AGPL-3.0 guarantees it:

* Any copy, fork or modified version you distribute must be licensed under the
  AGPL-3.0 as a whole, with its complete corresponding source code.
* If you run a (modified or unmodified) Privee server that other people use over
  a network, you must offer them the complete source code of the version you
  run (AGPL-3.0, section 13). Privee does this with the "Source code" link in
  the web interface and the `source_url` field of `GET /api/app/info`: set the
  PRIVEE_SOURCE_URL environment variable to your own repository when you deploy
  a fork.
* You may not add further restrictions, relicense the code under proprietary
  or non-copyleft terms, or incorporate it into closed-source software.

